hexagon: fuse MUL_MAT and ADD only when the ADD reads the whole product
Fold-into: patches/hexagon-fusion/0001-hexagon-htp-fused-matvec-add-read-src2-from-ddr.patch

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

Findings dsp-mm-add-shape and dsp-mm-add-src2 of fuzz-hexhost, task #155.
try_fuse_mul_mat_add fused a MUL_MAT and the ADD after it when one input of
the ADD had the data address of the product. Two conditions give an
incorrect fused op:

- dsp-mm-add-shape: the ADD reads the product through a view with fewer
  rows or columns at the same address. The fused kernel writes the full
  product into the smaller output of the ADD, thus it writes past that
  output.
- dsp-mm-add-src2: the other input of the ADD (src2 of the fused op) has a
  broadcast in dimension 0, or a dimension that ggml_add repeats. The fused
  kernels read full rows of src2 and broadcast only a dimension of size 1,
  thus they read past src2.

This patch fuses the two ops only when the ADD reads the whole product (the
same address, type, shape and strides), the output of the ADD has the shape
of the product, and src2 has full rows and, in each other dimension, a size
of 1 or the size of the product. The matcher is upstream code. The src2 read
of the fused kernels comes from hexagon-fusion/0001.

Evidence (2026-09-23):
- The regression inputs tests/fuzz/hexhost/regress/kparams/dsp-mm-add-
  shape.bin and dsp-mm-add-src2.bin give the finding before this patch (the
  model of the DSP kernels in the fake DSP of fuzz-hexhost) in the none,
  asan and ubsan builds, debug and release. With the five patches of
  fuzz-hexhost they give no finding in the asan build, debug and release.
- The kparams fuzzer with the conditions of tasks #155 and #159 on ran 6
  times for 100 s with the patches: no finding.
- The fused ops of the Qwen3.5 graphs are the same before and after (x86,
  the real-graph tool of fuzz-hexhost with the fake DSP). The count of each
  op kind of each graph is the same:
    2B decode   66 MUL_MAT_ADD, 30 MUL_MAT_NX, 73 RMS_NORM_MUL
    2B prefill  48 MUL_MAT_ADD, 30 MUL_MAT_NX, 73 RMS_NORM_MUL
    4B decode   88 MUL_MAT_ADD, 40 MUL_MAT_NX, 96 RMS_NORM_MUL
    4B prefill  88 MUL_MAT_ADD, 40 MUL_MAT_NX, 96 RMS_NORM_MUL
- The phone check of the five patches of fuzz-hexhost together (OnePlus 13,
  the 2B Q8_0 on HTP0, thermal status 0, cpu7 cap 4.32 GHz, battery 27.6 to
  27.7 °C, MemAvailable 8.9 to 9.5 GB):
  - test-backend-ops on HTP0 in five op groups (GATED_DELTA_NET and
    SSM_CONV, MUL_MAT_ID, CONCAT CPY GET_ROWS SET_ROWS, the binary ops with
    GLU and SOFT_MAX, NORM RMS_NORM SCALE): each group passes before and
    after.
  - llama-bench tg32 -r 3 after one warmup at 23.76 t/s: before 23.56 ±
    0.10, after 23.59 ± 0.27, before 23.63 ± 0.13, after 23.57 ± 0.11 t/s.
  - llama-speculative-simple with the MTP draft of depth 4, temperature 0,
    64 tokens: before 23.589 and 23.685 t/s, after 24.076 and 24.029 t/s.
    Each run accepts 44 drafts (52.381 %), and the four runs give the same
    text.

Measurement: the host instructions for each decode token of the 4B Q8_0
graph (x86, the real-graph tool with the fake DSP, perf stat, with
GGML_HEXAGON_BATCHCACHE=0): 3,711,938 before this patch and 3,709,475 after.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
index 7586c16..265d5c1 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
@@ -2843,14 +2843,35 @@ struct ggml_hexagon_opbatch {
 
         if (!ggml_hexagon_tensor_is_fuseable(mm_out)) return false;
 
+        // The ADD must read the whole product: the product itself, or a view with the same bytes,
+        // type, shape and strides. A view with fewer rows or columns starts at the same address,
+        // but the fused kernel writes the full product into the smaller output of the ADD.
+        auto is_whole_product = [mm_out](const ggml_tensor * t) {
+            return t == mm_out || (t->data == mm_out->data && t->type == mm_out->type &&
+                                   ggml_are_same_shape(t, mm_out) && ggml_are_same_stride(t, mm_out));
+        };
         const ggml_tensor * src2;
-        if (add_src0 == mm_out || add_src0->data == mm_out->data) {
+        if (is_whole_product(add_src0)) {
             src2 = add_src1;
-        } else if (add_src1 == mm_out || add_src1->data == mm_out->data) {
+        } else if (is_whole_product(add_src1)) {
             src2 = add_src0;
         } else {
             return false;
         }
+        if (!ggml_are_same_shape(node.dst(), mm_out)) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        // The fused kernels read full rows of src2 (ne[0] of the product) and broadcast only a
+        // dimension of size 1 (htp/matmul-ops.c:359, 472 and 3664-3667). ggml_add also permits a
+        // broadcast in dimension 0 and a repeat of a larger size, which the kernels read outside src2.
+        if (src2->ne[0] != mm_out->ne[0]) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        for (int i = 1; i < GGML_MAX_DIMS; i++) {
+            if (src2->ne[i] != 1 && src2->ne[i] != mm_out->ne[i]) {
+                return false;
+            }
+        }
 
         const ggml_tensor * src0 = last_node.src0();
         const ggml_tensor * src1 = last_node.src1();
